 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 457884,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "A certain type of COVID-related virus affects 5% of the population. A screening test is available to detect the virus. Assume the probability of a true positive from the screening test is 85%, meaning that the probability that a person has a positive test result, given that they actually have the virus, is 0.85. Also assume the probability of a false positive from the screening test is 12%, which indicates the probability that a person has a positive test result, given that they do not have the virus, is 0.12. Calculate the probability that a person actually has the virus given that the screening test shows a positive result. Round your answer to 3 decimal places.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "0.272 "
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "The following probabilities are known:<br>\n<span data-math=\"\\begin{aligned}P{\\left(\\mathrm A\\right)}&amp;=0.05\\\\P{\\left(\\mathrm A'\\right)}&amp;=0.95\\end{aligned}\"></span><br>The conditional probabilities can be interpreted as follows:<br><span data-math=\"P\\left( {B\\;|\\;A} \\right) = P{\\rm{(}}\\mathrm{positive}\\;\\mathrm{test}\\;\\mathrm{result}\\;{\\rm{|}}\\;\\mathrm{patient}\\;\\mathrm{has}\\;\\mathrm{virus}) = 0.85\"></span><br><span data-math=\"P\\left( {B\\;|\\;A'} \\right) = P{\\rm{(}}\\mathrm{positive}\\;\\mathrm{test}\\;\\mathrm{result}\\;{\\rm{|}}\\;\\mathrm{patient}\\;\\mathrm{does}\\;\\mathrm{not}\\;\\mathrm{have}\\;\\mathrm{the}\\;\\mathrm{virus}) = 0.12\"></span><br>Substituting these probabilities into the formula for Bayes’ Theorem results in the following:<br><span data-math=\"P{\\left(A\\;\\left|\\;\\right.\\right.}B)=\\frac{P{\\left(A\\right)}\\;\\cdot\\;P{\\left(B\\;\\left|\\;\\right.\\right.}A)}{P{\\left(A\\right)}\\;\\cdot\\; P{\\left(B\\;\\left|\\;\\right.\\right.}A)+P(A')\\;\\cdot\\; P(B\\;\\vert\\;A')}\"></span><br><span data-math=\"P{\\rm{(}}\\mathrm{patient}\\;\\mathrm{has}\\;\\mathrm{virus}\\;{\\rm{|}}\\;\\mathrm{positive}\\;\\mathrm{test}\\;\\mathrm{result}) = \\frac{{0.05\\;\\cdot\\;0.85}}{{0.05\\;\\cdot\\;0.85\\;+\\; 0.95\\;\\cdot\\;0.12}} = 0.272\"></span>"
    }
   ],
